---
// WHY-NEW-FILE: src/components/ConfidenceDetail.astro
//   CLOSEST-EXISTING: src/components/Confidence.astro
//   EXTENSION-COST: Confidence.astro derives its reason from `level` alone
//     (`confidenceReasonEs(level)`), so every row on the page reads the exact
//     same sentence for the same level -- twenty spots, one of three
//     canned paragraphs. No caller of that component can pass a per-row
//     reason without breaking its own declared contract (day-one confidence
//     is model agreement only, HANDOFF.md section 5). This component is the
//     new, honest shape: the reason travels in from the row that carries it.
//   PARALLEL-RATIONALE: a different data source (a prop, not a derivation)
//     and a second real caller once the cross-lane wiring lands (the ranked
//     rows and the spot-detail day sections), neither of which has any
//     reason to depend on a component that computes its own reason.
//
// The confidence disclosure: the level word beside the score, always
// visible; THIS row's own published reason, one tap away via native
// <details>/<summary>. Zero JavaScript (adr-publish-time-html-rendering.md)
// -- the browser's own disclosure widget does the work, no script ships.
//
// Rendering a reason this component invented, derived, or borrowed from
// another row would be worse than rendering nothing: every spot would carry
// a specific-sounding explanation computed for somebody else. So this
// component composes nothing. It takes the row's own reason as a prop and
// prints it, unmodified, or omits the block entirely when the row has none
// (the degrade path: a stated absence -- no disclosure to open -- never an
// empty box and never an invented sentence).
//
// `name="confidence"` makes every disclosure on the page an exclusive HTML5
// details group: opening one auto-closes any other already open, natively,
// no JS.
//
// The visible trigger reads the full "Confianza alta/media/baja" (see
// Confidence.astro's header for why a bare level word is not enough).
//
// No aria-label: the visible text already says the full phrase, and
// <summary>'s native disclosure-triangle semantics already announce the
// expand/collapse state, so adding one would double-announce both.
//
// Context-agnostic by construction (step 01-09): this component carries no
// <style> block and no assumption about an ancestor's layout, so it renders
// identically correct inside a ranked row (ol.ranked li) and inside a
// spot-page day section (section[data-day]). The ranked row's own
// grid-column placement (Confidence.astro's third-line decision) lives
// entirely in components.css, scoped to `ol.ranked li > details.confidence`
// -- never here -- so a day section with no grid ancestor simply flows in
// normal document order. Each mounted instance is driven only by its own
// `level`/`reason` props, so two instances never share state: today's
// section and tomorrow's section (or two ranked rows) each show their own
// word and their own reason, never one copied into the other. Verified with
// an isolated build harness mounting distinct level/reason instances inside
// section[data-day="today"], section[data-day="tomorrow"] and ol.ranked li
// in the same page: each block's compiled HTML carries only its own values.
// Do not add row-specific CSS (grid-column, positioning) inside this file or
// this guarantee breaks for the day-section case.
//
// Step 01-10: level reads by shape AND word, never by colour alone
// (09-design-system.md section 9, "confidence indicator" recipe: glyph dots
// beside the level word, no colour -- confidence is a certainty signal, not
// a quality verdict, and a green/amber treatment would visually collide with
// the go/stale vocabulary elsewhere on the page). CONFIDENCE_LEVEL_DOTS_ES
// renders the level as filled-of-three dots (baja one, media two, alta
// three -- section 5's own example confirms "media" is `●●○`),
// using the two font glyphs the recipe names (U+25CF/U+25CB, universal
// coverage, 0 bytes). The glyph span sits inside <summary>, after the word,
// `aria-hidden="true"` so it is never announced as a stray character (the
// full phrase already says the level; <summary>'s own disclosure semantics
// already announce open/closed) -- and specifically NOT a `::before`/
// `::after` CSS content string, because that would be invisible to
// `innerText` and therefore to anyone reading the rendered page's own text.
// No per-level colour is introduced anywhere in this file: the glyph
// characters carry the distinction by shape and count, inheriting whatever
// ink colour the summary already has, identically across levels.
import { CONFIDENCE_LEVEL_WORD_ES, type ConfidenceLevel } from '../scoring/confidence';

const CONFIDENCE_LEVEL_DOTS_ES: Readonly<Record<ConfidenceLevel, string>> = {
  low: '●○○',
  medium: '●●○',
  high: '●●●',
};

interface Props {
  level: ConfidenceLevel;
  /** THIS row's own published reason. Absent means no reason was published
   * for this (spot, day) -- the degrade path, never a fabricated one. */
  reason?: string;
}

const { level, reason } = Astro.props;
const word = CONFIDENCE_LEVEL_WORD_ES[level];
const dots = CONFIDENCE_LEVEL_DOTS_ES[level];
// An empty or whitespace-only reason degrades exactly like an absent one: a
// stated absence, never a silent empty box a surfer taps and finds blank
// (application-architecture.md section 7, P1's confidence_reason row).
const hasReason = reason !== undefined && reason.trim() !== '';
---

<details class="confidence" name="confidence" data-level={level}>
  <summary>Confianza {word} <span class="confidence-shape" aria-hidden="true">{dots}</span></summary>
  {hasReason && <div>{reason}</div>}
</details>
